1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,720
Treatment?

2
00:00:00,720 --> 00:00:03,865
Could you show us how to do it?

3
00:00:03,967 --> 00:00:04,474
Okay?

4
00:00:04,576 --> 00:00:04,880
We—

5
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:06,400
Let's show a cupping move.

6
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:10,500
As we said, we place the cups on my upper

7
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:14,400
back, then down to just above my waist.

8
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:19,147
Five cups on each side, plus one each.

9
00:00:19,147 --> 00:00:21,520
.. twelve in total.

10
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:27,040
As you move your right side this way, move your

11
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:29,239
hips the other way.

12
00:00:29,355 --> 00:00:32,480
They should feel separated.

13
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:34,766
They move in opposite directions.

14
00:00:34,833 --> 00:00:35,635
For example,

15
00:00:35,635 --> 00:00:36,839
this way, I twist.

16
00:00:36,906 --> 00:00:38,644
I'm not talking about you.

17
00:00:38,644 --> 00:00:42,639
People often get it wrong at first, swaying

18
00:00:42,639 --> 00:00:44,776
side to side like this.

19
00:00:44,869 --> 00:00:46,448
That's not right.

20
00:00:46,448 --> 00:00:46,704
Why?

21
00:00:46,768 --> 00:00:48,560
Your spine curves like an S.

22
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:50,864
When your upper body moves this way,

23
00:00:50,864 --> 00:00:52,592
counter it; when your lower

24
00:00:52,592 --> 00:00:54,448
body moves, counter that too.

25
00:00:54,448 --> 00:00:57,328
So you move in a crosswise pattern.

26
00:00:57,328 --> 00:01:03,088
With an S-curve, just do this and your body will adjust naturally.

27
00:01:03,088 --> 00:01:04,048
Like this.

28
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:08,880
This...

29
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:10,240
It's fun to twist.

30
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:14,140
To care for your spine, you can do this

31
00:01:14,140 --> 00:01:18,240
without cups—just sway from side to side.

32
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:24,525
As you sway, you can move your elbows up and down.

33
00:01:24,525 --> 00:01:27,448
This position targets this part of the spine.

34
00:01:27,448 --> 00:01:29,397
Raise your elbows a little to

35
00:01:29,397 --> 00:01:31,414
target this part of the spine.

36
00:01:31,414 --> 00:01:36,216
You can sway like this, or raise your arms and sway.

37
00:01:36,216 --> 00:01:38,721
Okay, this feels great and is good for the spine—

38
00:01:38,721 --> 00:01:41,227
...and a simple way to keep it in good shape.

39
00:01:41,227 --> 00:01:43,106
And next, please—

40
00:01:43,106 --> 00:01:46,028
Dr. Wu, show us the worm exercise.

41
00:01:46,028 --> 00:01:48,951
Let's show everyone the worm exercise.

42
00:01:48,951 --> 00:01:52,148
For this caterpillar exercise, straighten

43
00:01:52,148 --> 00:01:55,423
your arms, then twist your body like this.

44
00:01:55,423 --> 00:01:58,176
I'll demonstrate the twist standing

45
00:01:58,176 --> 00:02:00,851
up so you can see it more clearly.

46
00:02:00,851 --> 00:02:02,939
Then lie down and twist like this.

47
00:02:02,939 --> 00:02:07,741
As you twist, move your hips up and down.

48
00:02:07,741 --> 00:02:10,872
Keep both arms straight.

49
00:02:10,872 --> 00:02:15,047
First, press both feet downward.

50
00:02:15,047 --> 00:02:19,056
Move your hips up and down to twist your

51
00:02:19,056 --> 00:02:22,563
spine side to side, about 20 times.

52
00:02:22,563 --> 00:02:27,922
After that, flex both feet upward and sway again.

53
00:02:27,922 --> 00:02:31,969
You'll notice that flexing them up...

54
00:02:31,969 --> 00:02:38,791
...feels different from pressing them down—the stretch and muscle tension
change.

55
00:02:38,791 --> 00:02:44,548
This gives your whole spine a thorough adjustment.

56
00:02:44,548 --> 00:02:48,348
If you don't have scoliosis, this is a

57
00:02:48,348 --> 00:02:51,649
great way to care for your spine.

58
00:02:51,749 --> 00:02:52,649
Lastly...

59
00:02:52,649 --> 00:02:55,073
How do you do the hip sway with

60
00:02:55,073 --> 00:02:56,636
hands on your waist?

61
00:02:56,714 --> 00:02:57,340
Let's...

62
00:02:57,340 --> 00:03:00,751
Next, let's demonstrate the hands-on-hips sway.

63
00:03:00,751 --> 00:03:05,929
The key is to rest your calves on a raised

64
00:03:05,929 --> 00:03:10,984
cushion, about 20 to 30 centimeters high.

65
00:03:10,984 --> 00:03:14,599
Place your hands on your waist,

66
00:03:14,599 --> 00:03:18,446
around the top of your hip bones.

67
00:03:18,446 --> 00:03:23,350
Then sway your buttocks from side to side.

68
00:03:23,350 --> 00:03:26,438
After 10 side-to-side sways,

69
00:03:26,548 --> 00:03:32,944
move your hands up about two finger-widths and sway again.

70
00:03:32,944 --> 00:03:36,959
Do three rounds, alternating between

71
00:03:36,959 --> 00:03:40,193
the middle, above, and below.

72
00:03:40,193 --> 00:03:42,706
I'll demonstrate lying down.

73
00:03:42,706 --> 00:03:47,015
Put your hands on your waist and lift your hips.

74
00:03:47,015 --> 00:03:49,787
Then sway your hips from side to side.

75
00:03:49,787 --> 00:03:52,369
Use your waist under your hands as the pivot;

76
00:03:52,369 --> 00:03:54,607
move back and forth in a cross pattern.

77
00:03:54,607 --> 00:03:58,070
When you get tired, relax and lower

78
00:03:58,070 --> 00:04:01,830
your hips onto the bed, then continue.

79
00:04:01,830 --> 00:04:06,622
After the cross-pattern movement, move your hands up two finger-widths.

80
00:04:06,689 --> 00:04:12,763
Sway side to side there, then lower your hands and sway, then move them
up again and sway.

81
00:04:12,763 --> 00:04:16,390
Your hip bones at the waistline are roughly

82
00:04:16,390 --> 00:04:19,594
level with the lower lumbar vertebrae,

83
00:04:19,594 --> 00:04:23,305
around L3 to L5, where problems often occur.

84
00:04:23,305 --> 00:04:26,664
Swaying side to side helps loosen the

85
00:04:26,664 --> 00:04:31,020
muscles and tissues on either side of the spine.

86
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:33,652
This can open the hip joints.

87
00:04:33,652 --> 00:04:38,889
After opening it up, your bones can gradually return to place.

88
00:04:38,973 --> 00:04:45,561
But be careful: if this movement makes your lower-back pain or numbness
worse,

89
00:04:45,561 --> 00:04:50,961
it may not be right for you, so stop for now.

90
00:04:50,961 --> 00:04:57,080
After rocking for a while, your spine can gradually

91
00:04:57,080 --> 00:04:58,471
move back into place.

92
00:04:58,537 --> 00:04:59,531
Simple as that.

93
00:04:59,597 --> 00:05:00,789
Thank you, Dr. Wu—

94
00:05:00,789 --> 00:05:02,741
for that wonderful demonstration.

95
00:05:02,741 --> 00:05:05,879
To prevent scoliosis from worsening,

96
00:05:05,879 --> 00:05:09,104
what should patients watch out for in

97
00:05:09,104 --> 00:05:12,503
daily life, when lying down or sitting?

98
00:05:12,503 --> 00:05:15,585
What details should they pay special attention to?

99
00:05:15,585 --> 00:05:17,928
Could you give us some advice, Dr. Wu?

100
00:05:17,990 --> 00:05:18,360
First,

101
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:20,347
we should maintain good posture.

102
00:05:20,409 --> 00:05:21,093
Actually...

103
00:05:21,093 --> 00:05:27,263
Scoliosis isn't necessarily caused by poor posture.

104
00:05:27,263 --> 00:05:29,558
It's strange—it progresses very

105
00:05:29,558 --> 00:05:31,558
quickly during adolescence.

106
00:05:31,558 --> 00:05:35,298
Even without poor posture, good posture can

107
00:05:35,298 --> 00:05:39,213
indeed help prevent scoliosis from worsening.

108
00:05:39,213 --> 00:05:41,454
So that's something to keep in mind.

109
00:05:41,454 --> 00:05:45,614
Also, don't hold the same posture for too long.

110
00:05:45,614 --> 00:05:49,598
Even with good posture, people with scoliosis

111
00:05:49,598 --> 00:05:53,404
can get uncomfortable if they sit too long.

112
00:05:53,404 --> 00:05:56,801
Since their posture is already uneven,

113
00:05:56,801 --> 00:06:01,807
they should get up and move around or stretch regularly.

114
00:06:01,807 --> 00:06:03,490
Also, watch your sleeping position;

115
00:06:03,490 --> 00:06:04,981
avoid sleeping on your stomach.

116
00:06:04,981 --> 00:06:08,902
Sleeping on your stomach puts pressure on your neck.

117
00:06:08,902 --> 00:06:13,174
It can also make your thoracic spine curve downward,

118
00:06:13,174 --> 00:06:17,118
causing problems and worsening spinal alignment.

119
00:06:17,118 --> 00:06:20,892
Also avoid carrying heavy loads.

120
00:06:20,892 --> 00:06:26,080
They put strain on your body, so be careful.

121
00:06:26,080 --> 00:06:33,736
You may also need to avoid certain sports, such as long-distance running,
ballet, gymnastics, and even swimming.

122
00:06:33,736 --> 00:06:37,279
You might think swimming is symmetrical

123
00:06:37,279 --> 00:06:40,458
and helps balance the spine, right?

124
00:06:40,458 --> 00:06:44,956
Here's why: swimming is a symmetrical movement for

125
00:06:44,956 --> 00:06:47,655
people with scoliosis, whether

126
00:06:47,655 --> 00:06:50,354
freestyle or breaststroke, but

127
00:06:50,354 --> 00:06:53,604
scoliosis causes uneven strength,

128
00:06:53,604 --> 00:06:56,262
so one arm may work harder.

129
00:06:56,262 --> 00:07:01,284
This creates muscle imbalance, which can eventually

130
00:07:01,284 --> 00:07:04,924
make scoliosis worse rather than help.

131
00:07:04,924 --> 00:07:08,372
It may even progress, so be careful.

132
00:07:08,372 --> 00:07:12,552
Finally, change your diet and get enough nutrients.

133
00:07:12,552 --> 00:07:16,629
Research shows that people who are underweight often

134
00:07:16,629 --> 00:07:20,706
also have low bone density, and may be more prone to

135
00:07:20,706 --> 00:07:21,490
scoliosis.

136
00:07:21,568 --> 00:07:24,547
Studies found that 27 to 38 percent of

137
00:07:24,547 --> 00:07:28,873
Women with scoliosis often have low bone density.

138
00:07:28,873 --> 00:07:31,521
For severe cases, the rate may

139
00:07:31,521 --> 00:07:33,110
be as high as 47%.

140
00:07:33,198 --> 00:07:33,816
Dr. Wu,

141
00:07:33,816 --> 00:07:37,617
Today’s discussion of scoliosis was fascinating and

142
00:07:37,617 --> 00:07:38,362
practical.

143
00:07:38,436 --> 00:07:41,268
Could you briefly summarize it for us?

144
00:07:42,592 --> 00:07:43,062
Sure.

145
00:07:43,156 --> 00:07:46,821
Scoliosis treatment can be complicated.

146
00:07:46,821 --> 00:07:50,673
As we mentioned, if your curve is severe,

147
00:07:50,673 --> 00:07:54,432
see a specialist in scoliosis correction

148
00:07:54,432 --> 00:07:57,712
for treatment, preferably without surgery.

149
00:07:57,872 --> 00:08:01,792
If these three methods we discussed help you...
